              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दुखाना — dukhānā — \"to hurt someone's feelings\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मीरा ने कड़वी बात कहकर अपनी माँ का दिल दुखाया। Mīrā ne kaṛvī bāt kahkar apnī māṁ kā dil dukhāyā. Mira hurt her mother's feelings with a harsh remark."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने दिल दुखाया, usne dil dukhāyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दुखाना (dukhānā) is a tadbhava: CDIAL lists Hindi dukhānā, the causative, beside dukhnā, \"to ache\", under Sanskrit duḥkhati, \"pains\" (CDIAL 6376). dil dukhānā, \"to make the heart ache\", is the usual phrase."
            }
          ]
